invariant: INV-17
file: sha512_avx2.h
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh sha512-stack
reason: SHA512_AVX2_BELOW_LEN, the bytes of stack sha512_hw.c wipes below
  each call of the AVX2 kernel, is 240. That covers the 208 or 224 bytes
  sha512_avx2_compress_blocks writes below its caller under gcc 13.3 and
  the 16 more the test asks for, so the lane's sha512-avx2 part, a gcc
  build, passes. Under clang for x86-64 the kernel writes 256 or 272
  bytes, and the wipe leaves a word the call computed from its message
  below it. build.zig builds the object with clang. The lane's sha512-stack part
  builds bin/sha2_equiv_test with clang for x86-64 and runs it under
  qemu-x86_64, where it measures the kernel's depth against the length
  and then finds a word. The lane skips without docker, and this then
  reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
#define SHA512_AVX2_BELOW_LEN 512
--- new
#define SHA512_AVX2_BELOW_LEN 240
